# Line-ending policy.
#
# Why this file exists: `core.autocrlf=true` is the Git for Windows default, and
# without these rules it rewrites LF -> CRLF on checkout for anything it decides
# is "text". A LightGBM .txt model is text by that heuristic and binary in
# practice -- its parser is strict about line structure, and a stray CR makes it
# fail with "Model format error, expect a tree here" and then abort the process.
#
# That is not hypothetical: all 12 models in prediction_bundle/models/ were
# unloadable on a Windows checkout while being perfectly clean in the Git blob,
# so the corruption was invisible to anyone inspecting the repository and fatal
# to anyone actually running it. A Docker image built from a Windows checkout
# inherits the corrupted files too.

# Normalise text in the repo, and let Git decide checkout endings for the rest.
* text=auto

# Model artefacts: never touch these bytes.
*.txt binary
prediction_bundle/models/*.txt binary

# Data and archives.
*.csv binary
*.csv.gz binary
*.gz binary
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pkl binary
*.pt binary
*.bin binary
*.pdf binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they break when run in a Linux container --
# `/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter`.
*.sh text eol=lf
infra/docker/*.sh text eol=lf
infra/aws/*.sh text eol=lf

# Files whose format depends on exact bytes.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Notebooks are JSON; keep them diffable but stable.
*.ipynb text eol=lf
